    "created_at": "2021-11-25T09:17:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-25T09:17:00Z",
    "body": "The other problem is that it can contain essentially any header value byte, which historically has been an attack vector (and is why we have restrictions on the other headers now).\r\n\r\nWe'd have to apply the same restrictions as with `accept`.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
